        "original_id": "97854127-4559-5d83-b54d-e7a69cb1a028",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: We Were Soldiers, We Were Soldiers Once… And Young\n- People: Hal Moore\n- Roles: Lieutenant General, brigadier general, major general\n- Awards: Distinguished Service Cross\n- Organizations: U.S. military, West Point\n\nFacts:\n- In 1992, Hal Moore was identified as a Lieutenant General (Ret.) and as a co-author source for the book We Were Soldiers Once… And Young, which We Were Soldiers is based on.\n- Hal Moore received the Distinguished Service Cross, the U.S. military's second-highest decoration for valor.\n- Hal Moore was the first member of West Point's class of 1945 to be promoted to brigadier general, then major general, and then lieutenant general.",
